# Shared wire

Client and server compile the same structs in the same order. A second
copy will drift. A field in the middle shifts every later value into
garbage, silently.

- Append fields at the end of `PlayerEntity` / `VehicleEntity`.
- Position / velocity / rotation stay on `NetworkEntity`. Do not
  re-declare them.
- Transitions that play once (enter, exit, shot, reload, death, bystander
  damage) are reliable RPCs in `code/shared/rpc/`.
- `applyRatios` on `VehicleDamageReport` must stay false for status-only
  reports or every door slams shut.
- After any serialize change, restart the server **and** both clients.
